<ttl id="1002K_S000B_74229_T002J" variety="T002J">
<name>Cooler Thermistor NO.1</name>
<para id="RM000000FIO00FX" category="G" type-id="3001K" name-id="52281-00" from="200612">
<name>Component Inspection</name>
<subpara id="RM000000FIO00FX_01" type-id="01" category="01">
<s-1 id="RM000000FIO00FX_01_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___000016I00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Cooler Thermistor NO.1</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E147894J01" width="2.775699831in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
<s2>
<ptxt>Cooler Thermistor NO.1 Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>The cooler thermistor NO.1 is a non-reusable part, so inspect it while it is attached to the cooler evaporator NO.1.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the connector terminals.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry morerows="8" valign="middle">
<ptxt>1 - 2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>-10°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>7.30 to 9.10 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>-5°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>5.65 to 6.95 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>0°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>4.40 to 5.35 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>5°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>3.40 to 4.15 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>10°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2.70 to 3.25 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>15°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2.14 to 2.58 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>20°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1.71 to 2.05 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>25°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1.38 to 1.64 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>30°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1.11 to 1.32 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Touching the temperature sensor part allows body heat to affect it and prevents a correct judgment, so hold the connector side when inspecting the sensor.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Allow the sensor to adjust to the ambient temperature before inspecting.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
</subpara>
</para>
